course: dictionary
lesson: 990
title: Bodily: to do with the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bodily has two jobs. As an adjective it means to do with the body, like bodily needs or bodily harm. As an adverb it means by moving or lifting the whole body, as in «He was carried bodily out of the room.»
explain: Use the words around it to find the meaning. In «bodily harm», harm is something done to a person, so bodily tells you it is harm to the body. In «carried bodily out of the room», the person was lifted and taken out whole, so bodily means with the whole body.
explain: The sentence «Christians believe Jesus rose bodily from death and is alive» uses bodily in the same way, meaning with the whole body. The sentence tells you what some people believe, so you can understand the word without deciding whether the belief is true.
fact: Bodily means to do with the body, such as bodily needs or bodily harm.
fact: As an adverb, bodily means by moving or lifting the whole body, as in «He was carried bodily out of the room».
fact: In science and health lessons, bodily functions include breathing, digestion and going to the toilet.
fact: Bodily fluids include blood, sweat and spit.
fact: In legal and formal texts, «grievous bodily harm» means serious injury.
exercise: «He was carried bodily out of the room.» What does bodily mean here? | Slowly, one step at a time | Only a little bit | *With the whole body, lifted and moved | Very quietly
exercise: Which phrase means to do with the body? | a loud noise | a long journey | a sunny day | *bodily needs
exercise: In a science lesson, which is a bodily function? | A grey, wet day | A castle | *Breathing | A bicycle
test: «Grievous bodily harm» means what? | Cold weather | Very small cuts | A happy party | *Serious injury
test: Which of these is a bodily fluid? | Gravel | *Sweat | Paper | Sunshine
exam: In «Christians believe Jesus rose bodily from death», what does bodily mean? | Quietly and softly | To do with a shop | *With the whole body | Only just
